1. Definitions

"Licensor" means the copyright holder(s) who make the Software available under this License.

"Software" means the source code and associated materials expressly made available under this License, excluding third-party materials governed by their own licenses.

"Covered Code" means copyright-protected code from the Software, including recognizable adaptations of that code, but not independent implementations of its ideas, functionality, methods, or interfaces.

"Derived Project" means a project containing Covered Code, whether copied or adapted.

"Independent Distribution" means publishing, offering, supplying, or making available a Derived Project as a separate product, mod, library, downloadable package, or software release. A Development Fork as defined below is not an Independent Distribution.

"Development Fork" means a repository fork or copy maintained to inspect, test, modify, collaborate on, or propose contributions to the Software, clearly identifying the Original Repository and not promoted or released as an independent substitute for the Software.

"Substantial Modification" means a genuine and material technical contribution that meaningfully changes, improves, or extends the Software's capabilities, functionality, architecture, performance, reliability, security, accessibility, or other practical behavior. Substantial Modification is assessed in the context of the Software as a whole, based on the significance of the changes rather than their number, size, or percentage of source code.

"Standalone Rebranding" means an Independent Distribution of a Derived Project that is primarily a republished edition, replacement, or substitute for the Software and does not contain Substantial Modifications, regardless of the project's name, branding, or stated authorship.

